A||N||6||Bigfieroman||Accellerated rear tire wear?||||5||
Z||000000||Bigfieroman||08-03-2001||01:51 PM||||I have Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 225/50-16s in the rear of my auto gt, I am experiencing some really fast tire wear.  I don't peel tire, but I do drive the car hard.  The fronts look almost new and were installed at the same time.  Is the tire wear normal for an 87'?  Would it help if I put a swaybar back there?  Is this something everyone encounters?  Please tell me if this is normal or if the tires are defective.  Btw, they are ZR  trac AA temp A treadwear 280.  The guy from tire rack said they should last 20k when I bought them.  Thanks all.<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||5
Z||000001||watts||08-03-2001||02:19 PM||||It is normal for a Fiero to run the rear tires off at a ratio of 2-1 over the front. You have to options rotat the tires or just replace the rears twice as quick as the front.  At least that is what I found it happens for me.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||08-03-2001||02:39 PM||||280 tread wear is not all that high. I'd rotate them regularly, but with 280 tread wear, I'd expect them to be down to the indicators by 25k miles.<P>I have Kumho's on might 86SC so I'll see how they wear. I believe mine are 340 wear.<P>Are they wearing evenly across the tread?<P>I will say that several of us here are trying them and the tread wear conversation does come up.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 08-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||08-03-2001||04:29 PM||||Are the back wheels aligned properly? I had an 85 GT that was misaligned (from the factory). Cupped the edges of the tires. Wore 'em out in a big hurry. Sounded like a 4X4 going down the road, too.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||08-03-2001||05:52 PM||||I've also experienced much faster rear tire wear on my '86 GT. The tires, Michelin XGT V4 (205/60-15 (f) and 215/60-15 (r)) looked NEW at about 33K miles, when I bought the car.  The rears are now pretty much gone (worn evenly) at 41K miles.  Rather disappointing since I drive moderately to slowly! <P>I'm considering BFG Comp T/As or Dunlop D60A2s as replacements.  Anyone have any comments or preferences?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Two88GTs||08-04-2001||11:28 AM||||Oh good!  I thought I was the only one having this problem with rears wearing out much faster.  I also don't drive my car that hard, but the rears(Dunlop D60A2 JLBs) on my black 88GT lasted maybe 15k before I replaced them.<BR>The fronts(also D60A2 JLBs) now have 16k and look as if they'll last about 40-45k.  I installed Comp T/A HR-4s on the rear this time, we'll see how long these last.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||08-04-2001||12:48 PM||||Sounds like us Fiero owners are accepting this fact of life better than the NSX owners did!<BR>Remember that fiasco?<BR>||||reg||1
